From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ninad Naik <ninanaik@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu: add qcom secure_vmid field to arm_smmu_domain

Add a per-domain u32 secure_vmid slot so a Qualcomm SMMU vendor
implementation can record the secure VMID a context bank is bound
to (parsed from the "qcom,iommu-vmid" DT property). The value is
consumed by the secure page-table allocator added in a follow-up
patch (qcom_alloc_pages / qcom_free_pages).

Signed-off-by: Ninad Naik <ninanaik@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu.h | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu.h b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu.h
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu.h
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu.h
@@ -385,6 +385,14 @@ struct arm_smmu_domain {
 	struct mutex			init_mutex; /* Protects smmu pointer */
 	spinlock_t			cb_lock; /* Serialises ATS1* ops and TLB syncs */
 	struct iommu_domain		domain;
+	/*
+	 * Use to store parse vmid value for those clients which want HLOS
+	 * to share pgtable to different entity(VMID).
+	 * Fix Me: Ideally this should be implemented on arm-smmu vendor
+	 * implementation driver, but as per current design of
+	 * arm_smmu_domain_alloc there is no way to call implementation callbacks.
+	 */
+	u32				secure_vmid;
 };
 
 struct arm_smmu_master_cfg {

